[agent:result] ===== create-experiment =====
[agent:result] Create experiment.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   Creates an experiment with a name. Returns the ID of the newly created
[agent:result]   experiment. Validates that another experiment with the same name does not
[agent:result]   already exist and fails if another experiment with the same name already
[agent:result]   exists.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   Throws RESOURCE_ALREADY_EXISTS if an experiment with the given name exists.
[agent:result]   Note: In some contexts, this error may be remapped to ALREADY_EXISTS. To be
[agent:result]   safe, clients should check for both error codes.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   Arguments:
[agent:result]     NAME: Experiment name.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] Usage:
[agent:result]   databricks experiments create-experiment NAME [flags]
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] Flags:
