[agent:result] ===== log-metric =====
[agent:result] Log a metric for a run.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   Log a metric for a run. A metric is a key-value pair (string key, float value)
[agent:result]   with an associated timestamp. Examples include the various metrics that
[agent:result]   represent ML model accuracy. A metric can be logged multiple times.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   Arguments:
[agent:result]     KEY: Name of the metric.
[agent:result]     VALUE: Double value of the metric being logged.
[agent:result]     TIMESTAMP: Unix timestamp in milliseconds at the time metric was logged.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] Usage:
[agent:result]   databricks experiments log-metric KEY VALUE TIMESTAMP [flags]
[agent:result] 
