[agent:result] ===== log-batch =====
[agent:result] Log a batch of metrics/params/tags for a run.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   Logs a batch of metrics, params, and tags for a run. If any data failed to be
[agent:result]   persisted, the server will respond with an error (non-200 status code).
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   In case of error (due to internal server error or an invalid request), partial
[agent:result]   data may be written.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   You can write metrics, params, and tags in interleaving fashion, but within a
[agent:result]   given entity type are guaranteed to follow the order specified in the request
[agent:result]   body.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   The overwrite behavior for metrics, params, and tags is as follows:
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   * Metrics: metric values are never overwritten. Logging a metric (key, value,
[agent:result]   timestamp) appends to the set of values for the metric with the provided key.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   * Tags: tag values can be overwritten by successive writes to the same tag
[agent:result]   key. That is, if multiple tag values with the same key are provided in the
[agent:result]   same API request, the last-provided tag value is written. Logging the same tag
[agent:result]   (key, value) is permitted. Specifically, logging a tag is idempotent.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   * Parameters: once written, param values cannot be changed (attempting to
[agent:result]   overwrite a param value will result in an error). However, logging the same
[agent:result]   param (key, value) is permitted. Specifically, logging a param is idempotent.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   Request Limits ------------------------------- A single JSON-serialized API
[agent:result]   request may be up to 1 MB in size and contain:
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   * No more than 1000 metrics, params, and tags in total
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   * Up to 1000 metrics
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   * Up to 100 params
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   * Up to 100 tags
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   For example, a valid request might contain 900 metrics, 50 params, and 50
[agent:result]   tags, but logging 900 metrics, 50 params, and 51 tags is invalid.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   The following limits also apply to metric, param, and tag keys and values:
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   * Metric keys, param keys, and tag keys can be up to 250 characters in length
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   * Parameter and tag values can be up to 250 characters in length
